# Agent gate (priority 0)

**Loads first.** This file is **workflow only** — run order, checkboxes, when `vision/` edits are blocked. **Policy lives elsewhere; do not copy it here.**

| Read | For |
|------|-----|
| **`1_coding-rules.mdc`** | ① Plan → ④ Write; audit |
| **`2_lexicon.mdc`** | Token / Forbidden definitions — audit or explicit coinage only; not a ③ write-time checklist |

Checkboxes live **only in this file**. Each step: execute per **`1_coding-rules.mdc`** §①–④, then flip the matching checkbox when turn evidence below is satisfied.

## When this file applies

**Must run ①→②→③→④:** this turn will **modify** any path under `vision/` (`Write`, `StrReplace`, `Delete`, or equivalent).

**Skip ①–④ entirely (do not edit checkboxes here):** read-only; reply-only; shell/git with no `vision/` code change; edits only outside `vision/` and this turn does not change `vision/` code.

## Agent mode — mandatory sequence

**Before the first `vision/` code edit in this turn:**

1. Read this file, then **`1_coding-rules.mdc`** §①–④ (and **`2_lexicon.mdc`** only if audit or coinage).
2. StrReplace every `- [x]` below to `- [ ]`.
3. Do ① per **`1_coding-rules.mdc`** → StrReplace **only** ① to `- [x]`.
4. Do ② → StrReplace **only** ② to `- [x]`.
5. Do ③ → StrReplace **only** ③ to `- [x]`.
6. **First `vision/` code edit allowed only after ①②③ are `- [x]`.**
7. Do ④ → StrReplace **only** ④ to `- [x]`.

**Before every later `vision/` code edit in this turn:** ①②③④ must all be `- [x]` for the current function cycle.

**New function:** StrReplace ②③④ to `- [ ]`; redo ②→③→ `[x]`; edit; ④→ `[x]`. ① stays `- [x]` once per task.

**Forbidden (gate mechanics only):** any `vision/` code edit while ① or ② or ③ is `- [ ]`; two `- [x]` in one message; claim done while any checkbox is `- [ ]`; mark any checkbox `[x]` without matching turn evidence below. If **`1_coding-rules.mdc`** says a step is incomplete (e.g. ① **Files**), leave that checkbox `- [ ]` — do not edit `vision/`.

## Checkbox evidence (no performative `[x]`)

**① is `- [x]` only when** the same turn prose covers every bullet in **`1_coding-rules.mdc`** §①.

**② is `- [x]` only when** the same turn includes:
- same-**layer** sibling path you **Read in full** (not Grep-only);
- at least one `` `path:start-end` `` cite;
- chosen action: **extend** | **replace** | **inline**.

**③ is `- [x]` only when** the same turn prose covers the edit surface per **`1_coding-rules.mdc`** §③: each binding → sibling cite or inline; each bad-binding fix → delete + inline. **Defer** cites ①.

**④ is `- [x]` only when** the same turn confirms the diff passes **`1_coding-rules.mdc`** §④.

**Missing evidence = checkbox stays `- [ ]`; do not edit `vision/`.**

## Ask mode

Planning answers about `vision/` code: ①② per **`1_coding-rules.mdc`** in prose; mark `[x]` in reply text only; do not edit checkboxes here; skip ③④.

**Audit:** report ①–④ per **`1_coding-rules.mdc`** §Audit. Lexicon-only grep is **not** a completed audit.

